<title>MEXICO: Mexico silver output up, other metals detailed.</title>
<headline>Mexico silver output up, other metals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest silver producer, saw output rise 0.85 percent in the first seven months of the year to 1,467,138 kilos against the January-July period in 1995, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of metals and minerals production in the first seven months follows:</p>
<p>    Product     Jul 96     Jul 95     Jan-Jul   Pct Chge Vs 95</p>
<p>    Gold	   1,772	1,741	12,719	  16.6</p>
<p>    Silver     187,242    219,500   1,467,138	   0.85</p>
<p>    Lead	  14,523     16,147	94,978	 -13.8</p>
<p>    Copper	27,342     30,668     189,817	  -0.8</p>
<p>    Zinc	  27,823     33,501     196,604	  -2.0</p>
<p>    Coal	 826,338    470,751   4,811,505	  29.4</p>
<p>    Iron	 510,073    318,398   3,486,909	  13.1</p>
<p>    Sulphur     78,611     77,285     562,054	   8.9</p>
<p>    Dolomite    75,480     45,700     539,902	   n/a</p>
<p>    Gypsum     270,921    258,915   1,990,908	  -6.8</p>
<p>    Phosphorite 58,119     52,200     400,507	   n/a</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals output in kilos, others in tonnes.</p>
<p>Coal output in mineral volume. Figures revised from</p>
<p>January-July figures given by INEGI.</p>
<p>-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289560.</p>
</text>
